{"title":"Palindrome Partitioning IV","difficulty":"Hard","statement":"Given a string `s` of lowercase English letters, decide whether it can be split into **exactly three non-empty** substrings such that every one of the three substrings is a palindrome. The substrings must be contiguous and, concatenated in order, must give back `s`.\n\nA palindrome reads the same forwards and backwards. Print `true` if such a split exists and `false` otherwise. If `s` has fewer than three characters the answer is `false`.\n\n**Follow-up:** The interviewer first asked for a direct solution and then wanted it optimised with a dynamic-programming table that answers \"is `s[i..j]` a palindrome?\" in constant time.","inputFormat":"A single line containing the string `s`.","outputFormat":"Print `true` or `false`.","constraints":["1 ≤ |s| ≤ 2000","`s` consists of lowercase English letters"],"examples":[{"input":"abcbdd","output":"true","explanation":"Split into \"a\", \"bcb\" and \"dd\": all three are palindromes."},{"input":"bcbddxy","output":"false","explanation":"The only palindromic suffix is \"y\", and with it the remaining \"bcbddx\" cannot be cut into two palindromes: \"b\" leaves \"cbddx\" and \"bcb\" leaves \"ddx\", neither of which is a palindrome."},{"input":"abc","output":"true","explanation":"Every single character is a palindrome, so \"a\", \"b\", \"c\" works."}],"tests":[{"input":"a","output":"false"},{"input":"ab","output":"false"},{"input":"aab","output":"true"},{"input":"aaa","output":"true"},{"input":"abca","output":"false"},{"input":"abcd","output":"false"},{"input":"abab","output":"false"},{"input":"aaaa","output":"true"},{"input":"aabb","output":"true"},{"input":"abba","output":"true"},{"input":"cbabacbaaabcaaa","output":"false"},{"input":"aaaaaaabbbbaba","output":"true"},{"input":"aaababbabaa","output":"true"},{"input":"aa","output":"false"},{"input":"cbcacabbaccabbbbbb","output":"false"},{"input":"aaaaaabaaaabbab","output":"true"},{"input":"c","output":"false"},{